<decompilertest>
<binaryimage arch="x86:LE:64:default:gcc">
<!--
    kuna issue testcase: Thumb-1 switches through libgcc's case helpers in a
    stripped image.

    Stage:      P0 knowledge - the call-fixup installer recognizes the helpers
                by their instructions
                (`analyzers/callfixup/kuna_thumb1casesig.rs`), so the
                `switch*_r0` call-fixups apply at P2 flow.

    The XML wrapper only provides the harness architecture.  The script loads
    `thumb1case_le32` (source `thumb1case_le32.s` beside it, build commands in
    its header): a stripped Cortex-M0 ELF whose `_start` calls five
    dispatchers, each `cmp r0,#n; bhi default; bl helper` with the case table
    after the call, one per libgcc helper: unsigned byte (0x200dc, five cases
    returning 10..14), signed byte (0x20104, case 0 before the table, 20..23),
    unsigned halfword (0x20128, 30..33), signed halfword (0x2014e, case 0
    before the table, 40..42) and word (0x20170, 50..52).

    Before, the helpers had no name and the call read as an ordinary call that
    returns into the table: each dispatcher decompiled to one call and the
    first case.  Now every helper is named and tagged with its fixup, and each
    dispatcher is a switch over all of its cases.  The word helper's fixup
    adds the entry to the word-aligned table address (it used to scale the
    entry by four and add it to the return address).
-->
</binaryimage>
<script>
  <com>clear architecture</com>
  <com>load file crates/unlace-analysis/tests/fixtures/thumb1case_le32</com>
  <com>read symbols</com>
  <com>lo fu sub_200dc</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>lo fu sub_20104</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>lo fu sub_20128</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>lo fu sub_2014e</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>lo fu sub_20170</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>quit</com>
</script>
<stringmatch name="KUNA-THUMB1CASE #1: each dispatcher is a switch" min="5" max="5">switch\(a0\)</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="KUNA-THUMB1CASE #2: no helper call survives" min="0" max="0">sub_20(198|1aa|1bc|1d0|1e4)\(</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="KUNA-THUMB1CASE #3: the unsigned byte table reads its last case" min="1" max="1">return 0xe;</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="KUNA-THUMB1CASE #4: the signed byte table reaches the case before it" min="1" max="1">return 0x14;</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="KUNA-THUMB1CASE #5: the unsigned halfword table reads its last case" min="1" max="1">return 0x21;</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="KUNA-THUMB1CASE #6: the signed halfword table reaches the case before it" min="1" max="1">return 0x28;</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="KUNA-THUMB1CASE #7: the word table reads its later cases" min="2" max="2">return 0x3[34];</stringmatch>
</decompilertest>
